## FEATURES (context)
A. Stabilizer (Stable Stroke): slider 0..100 in Settings > 3D Brush. Smooths the pointer in SCREEN space before raycasting
   (so the stroke stays on the guide surface). Max smoothing factor = 0.75. Not stored per stroke.
B. Eyedropper tool (new toolbar tool "pick"): tap near a stroke -> copies its color, size, opacity and pressure response into the
   current brush (acts as Eyedropper + Injector), then switches back to the Brush tool.
C. Brush presets: "Save current brush" in Settings, tap a preset to apply, ✕ deletes. Max 8. Persisted in localStorage.
D. ActionBar button "Brush": applies the current brush (color, size, opacity, pressure) to the SELECTED strokes (one undo step).

